  "slug": "furdu",
  "name": "Furry Down Under",
  "shortName": "Furdu",
  "description": "Furry Down Under (FurDU) is an annual furry convention on the Gold Coast, Queensland, and the largest furry convention in Australia. It runs for three days, with an informal pre-con meetup on the Thursday since 2013. The first FurDU was held April 23 to 25, 2010, at the Vibe Hotel in Surfers Paradise, and was the first furry convention on the Gold Coast. It was founded by Oz Kangaroo and FlameDrake, and since 2015 it has been owned and run by Furry Down Under, Inc., a non-profit association with an elected committee. It later moved to the Watermark Hotel, the Outrigger Hotel and the Mantra on View. Fursuit games, a fursuit walk and fursuit photography have been part of it since the start, along with a growing Headless Lounge. Attendance has grown from 92 to over 2,100 in 2026.",
